    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince the value is derived purely from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate` (no external state), I followed the codebase's established idiom for derived read-only fields \u2014 the computed getters `getDisplayName()` / `getInitials()` on `Person`, which MapStruct projects into the DTO \u2014 rather than the assigned-at-creation pattern used for `customerCode` (which depends on the mutable owner count and is stored as a column).\n\nTwo focused changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a computed `getMembershipNumber()` getter that formats the two existing fields, guarding against nulls (legacy/seed owners lack a customer code and registration date) so it never NPEs on read. `%02d` correctly zero-pads years like 2007 \u2192 `07`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct auto-maps `getMembershipNumber()` into it \u2014 no mapper or controller changes needed.\n\nNote `registrationDate` is only defaulted at `@PrePersist`, so computing on read (rather than assigning in the controller before save) is what keeps the value correct \u2014 reinforcing the getter approach over an eager assignment.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes and the full suite builds green.",
